class:: OnsetRate
summary:: Rolling onset density
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Rhythm
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/BeatTrack3

description::
Counts rising-edge onset events in a bounded trailing timestamp window, divided by the full window duration. Startup therefore ramps naturally as events accumulate.

This is an independent implementation of the statistical definition above. Output updates at the server control rate; beat boundaries are quantized to a control block. Silence produces zero level/density or missing tempo evidence. No corpus-level accuracy is implied.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: trig
Control-rate trigger. Only nonpositive-to-positive transitions count as events.

argument:: windowTime
Trailing history in seconds. Rhythm analysis accepts 0.5–16, default 6; onset/tempo statistics accept 0.05–60, default 4.

argument:: minGap
Minimum seconds between accepted events, default zero.

returns::
Events per second.

examples::
OnsetRate counts detected rising-edge onset triggers over a rolling timestamp window to measure activity density in events per second. In this example, it drives an adaptive tube saturation effect: sparse beats remain clean and dynamic, while intense fills and rapid snare flurries drive the processor into aggressive harmonic distortion. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: tracks the real-time onset rate in events/second.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, 0.25);
        var onset = Onsets2.kr(chain, threshold: 0.15, fftSize: 1024, hop: 0.25);
        var rate = OnsetRate.kr(onset[0], windowTime: 2.0);
        var rateSmooth = rate.lag(0.04);

        // Saturation drive scaled by playing density
        var drive = (1.0 + (rateSmooth * 1.5)).clip(1.0, 8.0);
        var driven = (source * drive).tanh * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.2) + driven;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, rate) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Onset Rate", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 15.0, "events/s");
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

